{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAqZeBWDBbrrhBXPajRo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PcAvgjrAR42KHivDhfSt8V","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-UseNE6/ANSWER.md","content":"# Ticket #4471: no session replays for the new UI\n\n## Why\n\nSession replay on mobile is driven by the `PostHogWidget` wrapper. `posthog_flutter`\ncaptures screenshots from the subtree under that widget and sends them to the native\nSDK. Its docs say the app must be wrapped in `PostHogWidget` when\n`PostHogConfig.sessionReplay` is on (`lib/src/posthog_widget.dart` in\nposthog_flutter 5.55.0; the 5.36.3 copy has the same doc comment).\n\n- `lib/legacy_app.dart` wraps `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`. Replays work for the A/B group.\n- `lib/new_app.dart` returned `MaterialApp.router` with no wrapper. Replay was enabled\n  (`lib/analytics.dart`: `sessionReplay = true`) but there was no widget tree to capture.\n\nEvents still arrive for the new UI because the SDK is set up in `main.dart` and\n`PosthogObserver` is attached to the GoRouter, so screen events and custom events\n(`loan_amount_changed`, `application_submitted`) are unaffected. That matches the ticket.\n\n## Fix\n\n`lib/new_app.dart`: wrap `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget`, the same as `LegacyApp`.\nNo other changes. The `posthog_flutter` import was already present.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I did not run the app or check a recording in PostHog. `flutter analyze` could not run\n  because the package config is not resolved in this checkout. I ran `dart format` on the\n  file, which parses it.\n- The `phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI` project key in `lib/analytics.dart` is a CI placeholder and was left unchanged.\n- Confirm on a new-UI device build after the change that a recording appears in the Replay tab.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1083,"cache_read_input_tokens":33584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1083},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3e02be2-34ff-428f-8cae-a0bfa18013c6","uuid":"86c0976c-c1be-49b8-8944-7063d7b73d39","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:52:08.214Z","request_id":"req_011CgAqZdv7s87kofsrYwyLJ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PcAvgjrAR42KHivDhfSt8V":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-UseNE6/ANSWER.md","content":"# Ticket #4471: no session replays for the new UI\n\n## Why\n\nSession replay on mobile is driven by the `PostHogWidget` wrapper. `posthog_flutter`\ncaptures screenshots from the subtree under that widget and sends them to the native\nSDK. Its docs say the app must be wrapped in `PostHogWidget` when\n`PostHogConfig.sessionReplay` is on (`lib/src/posthog_widget.dart` in\nposthog_flutter 5.55.0; the 5.36.3 copy has the same doc comment).\n\n- `lib/legacy_app.dart` wraps `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`. Replays work for the A/B group.\n- `lib/new_app.dart` returned `MaterialApp.router` with no wrapper. Replay was enabled\n  (`lib/analytics.dart`: `sessionReplay = true`) but there was no widget tree to capture.\n\nEvents still arrive for the new UI because the SDK is set up in `main.dart` and\n`PosthogObserver` is attached to the GoRouter, so screen events and custom events\n(`loan_amount_changed`, `application_submitted`) are unaffected. That matches the ticket.\n\n## Fix\n\n`lib/new_app.dart`: wrap `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget`, the same as `LegacyApp`.\nNo other changes. The `posthog_flutter` import was already present.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I did not run the app or check a recording in PostHog. `flutter analyze` could not run\n  because the package config is not resolved in this checkout. I ran `dart format` on the\n  file, which parses it.\n- The `phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI` project key in `lib/analytics.dart` is a CI placeholder and was left unchanged.\n- Confirm on a new-UI device build after the change that a recording appears in the Replay tab.\n"}}}
