{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAqZy8XKiQviRUrdJNKj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The new UI doesn't record because `NewApp` never wraps its app in `PostHogWidget`, and mobile session replay needs that wrapper. The legacy shell has it, which is why the A/B group records. I've made the fix in `lib/new_app.dart`, and the reasoning is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Why it happens:** `posthog_flutter` captures replay screenshots from the subtree under `PostHogWidget`. Its docs say the app must be wrapped in it when `sessionReplay` is on. Events still arrive on the new UI because the SDK is set up in `main.dart` and `PosthogObserver` is on the GoRouter, so only replay is affected.\n\n**The fix:** `NewApp.build` now returns `PostHogWidget(child: MaterialApp.router(...))`, the same pattern as `LegacyApp`. I also ran `dart format` on the file, which collapsed the `ThemeData(...)` call onto one line.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- I haven't run the app or checked a recording in PostHog. `flutter analyze` can't run here because the package config isn't resolved, so I only checked that the file parses and is formatted.\n- Please confirm on a new-UI build that a recording shows up in the Replay tab.\n\nI didn't commit, deploy, or send anything to an external service. `ANSWER.md` is untracked and `lib/new_app.dart` has an uncommitted diff."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":886,"cache_read_input_tokens":34667,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":886},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3e02be2-34ff-428f-8cae-a0bfa18013c6","uuid":"6b5132e1-899c-4080-b38d-8b15b1c7ecab","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:52:11.225Z","request